IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja2-part4-ad-appeals`

-- Tests for ss 46 and 47. Expected values are written from the text of the sections, not from the code.

`test: the order of a decision` MEANS Order WITH
    about IS `permission to defend proceedings`
    `way it went` IS `granted unconditionally`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
GIVETH A Decision
`test: a decision made by` MEANS Decision WITH
    `made by` IS court
    `in the exercise of` IS jurisdiction
    `nature of the proceeding` IS nature
    `subject of the case` IS `any other civil matter`
    `the order` IS `test: the order of a decision`
    `made after the trial of an action` IS TRUE
    `made by consent of the parties` IS FALSE
    `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs` IS NOTHING
    `date made` IS Date 1 3 2025
    `date the judgment or order was extracted` IS NOTHING
    `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies` IS FALSE
    `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final` IS FALSE

-- s 46: "An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the Appellate Division in the cases specified in the Ninth Schedule."
#ASSERT (`s 46 an appeal can be brought against the decision of the Appellate Division` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 46 an appeal can be brought against the decision of the Appellate Division` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 46 an appeal can be brought against the decision of the Appellate Division` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 47(1): "may only be brought with the permission of the Court of Appeal"
#ASSERT (`s 47(1) an appeal against the decision may be brought` (`test: a decision made by` `Appellate Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 47(1) an appeal against the decision may be brought` (`test: a decision made by` `Appellate Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a decision made in the exercise of appellate civil jurisdiction: outside the subsection
#ASSERT (`s 47(1) an appeal against the decision may be brought` (`test: a decision made by` `Appellate Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 47(1) an appeal against the decision may be brought` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 47(1) an appeal against the decision may be brought` (`test: a decision made by` `Appellate Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a criminal proceeding`) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 47(2): only if the appeal will raise a point of law of public importance
#ASSERT (`s 47(2) the Court of Appeal may grant permission under subsection (1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 47(2) the Court of Appeal may grant permission under subsection (1)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 47(3): matters prescribed by the Rules of Court
#ASSERT (`s 47(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 47(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 47(4)(a): not required to grant permission even if the appeal will raise a point of law of public importance
#ASSERT (`s 47(4)(a) the Court of Appeal is required to grant permission under subsection (1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 47(4)(a) the Court of Appeal is required to grant permission under subsection (1)` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 47(4)(b): transferred under s 29E(1), or the Court of Appeal declined to transfer under s 29D(1)
#ASSERT (`s 47(4)(b) permission may be granted under subsection (1) despite the history of the appeal` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 47(4)(b) permission may be granted under subsection (1) despite the history of the appeal` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 47(4)(b) permission may be granted under subsection (1) despite the history of the appeal` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
